  "unit": "Unit 23 - Probability",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 23 - Probability for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Number&#x000A0;of&#x000A0;favorable&#x000A0;outcomes</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>Total&#x000A0;outcomes</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>certain&#x000A0;event</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>  </li>\n<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>impossible&#x000A0;event</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br />\nA fair die is rolled. What is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>rolling&#x000A0;a&#x000A0;4</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>?  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>not&#x000A0;</mtext><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br />\nProbability of rolling a 6 on a die is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.<br />\nProbability of not rolling a 6 is:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p>Events are independent if outcome of one does not affect the other.</p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>A</mi><mtext>&#x000A0;and&#x000A0;</mtext><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>&#x000B7;</mi><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong><br />\nFlip a coin and roll a die.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>Heads&#x000A0;and&#x000A0;a&#x000A0;3</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>&#x000B7;</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p>Events that cannot both occur.</p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>A</mi><mtext>&#x000A0;or&#x000A0;</mtext><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br />\nPick a card from a deck. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>Ace&#x000A0;or&#x000A0;King</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p>Use combinations or listing.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br />\nFrom 5 students (A,B,C,D,E), 1 is chosen at random.<br />\nProbability it’s A or B:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Decide if events are independent or mutually exclusive.  </li>\n<li>Watch for “at least one” → use complement rule.  </li>\n<li>In card/dice questions, always confirm total outcomes.  </li>\n<li>Reduce fractions!  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) A fair coin is flipped. Find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>Heads</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.<br />\n2) A bag has 3 red, 2 blue marbles. Pick one at random. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>Blue</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>?<br />\n3) Roll two dice. What’s <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>sum&#x000A0;=&#x000A0;7</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>?<br />\n4) A card is drawn from a deck. Find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mtext>spade&#x000A0;or&#x000A0;heart</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.<br />\n5) What is the probability of not rolling a 5 on a fair die?  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) Favorable outcomes: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> → 6 total.<br />\nTotal outcomes = 36.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>\n\n<p>4) Spades = 13, Hearts = 13.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>26</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>\n\n<p>5) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">\n</code></pre>",
